# Gnimu Monitor capture files and the vectors derived from them.
#
# These hold REAL GNSS fixes - committing them publishes the precise
# coordinates of wherever the capture was taken. They are also large (a few
# minutes at 20Hz is ~1MB) and personal to whoever recorded them.
#
# Keep captures and their vectors local. If a golden vector set is ever needed
# as a committed test fixture, sanitize it first (offset the coordinates and
# re-encode, so the packets stay self-consistent) rather than adding an
# exception here.
test/*.jsonl
test/vectors*.gc1
